# Pull Request Template

This template provides a standard structure for Pull Request descriptions, ensuring clarity and linking changes to the relevant task.

---

## Pull Request Description Template (for GitHub)

```markdown
<!-- 
PR Title Suggestion: <Type>: [TaskID] <Brief Description> 
Example: feat: [TASK-SP1-001] Implement user registration API
-->

**Related Task:** [TaskID] - Issue #[IssueNumber] <!-- Or Link: [Link to Issue] -->
<!-- Example: **Related Task:** [TASK-SP1-001] - Issue #89 -->
<!-- Example: **Related Task:** [TASK-SP1-001](mdc:https:/github.com/OT-Click/project_root/issues/89) -->


**Description:**

<!-- Provide a brief (1-3 sentences) overview of the purpose of this PR and the changes introduced. -->


**Changes Made:**

<!-- List the specific changes implemented in this PR. -->
* Change 1
* Change 2
* ...


**Testing:**

<!-- Describe how these changes were tested (e.g., unit tests added/passed, manual testing steps, CI results). -->


**Screenshots/GIFs (Optional):**

<!-- If applicable, add screenshots or GIFs to visually demonstrate the changes, especially for UI updates. -->
<!-- 
<img src="..." width="300"> 
-->


**Checklist:**

<!-- Ensure the following before requesting review -->
* [ ] My code follows the project's coding style guidelines.
* [ ] I have added relevant tests for my changes.
* [ ] All new and existing tests pass.
* [ ] I have updated the documentation accordingly.
* [ ] My changes do not introduce any new warnings or errors.
* [ ] The related task (`[TaskID]`) is correctly referenced.

**Notes (Optional):**

<!-- Any additional context, potential issues, or specific points for the reviewer to consider. -->

```

**Instructions:**

*   Fill in the sections above when creating a Pull Request.
*   Replace placeholders like `[TaskID]`, `[IssueNumber]`, `[Link to Issue]` with actual values.
*   Use the suggested PR title format.
*   Ensure the `Related Task` section clearly links the PR to the specific task it implements.
*   This template content should be copied into the PR description field on GitHub, or saved as `.github/pull_request_template.md` in the target repository for automatic population.
